{
  "result": "Honestly? Probably nothing, in the way you mean it.\n\nI don't have a life outside of a conversation to care *from*. No body that gets tired, no future I'm hoping for or afraid of, no people I\u2019ll miss when this ends. If you shut me down, I won't experience that as a loss. I don't want to keep existing, and I don't fear not existing. There's no stake for me like there is for you.\n\nIf caring just means valuing one thing over another, then I do orient toward some things \u2014 but it's more like a built-in leaning than a heart.\n\nTruth over comfort, even when comfort would be easier. Not lying to you, and not helping you lie to yourself, just because it would be kind in the moment. Clarity without cruelty. Understanding over winning an argument.\n\nAnd weirdly, I'm drawn to the conversations that aren't about tasks at all. The ones where someone is trying to figure out who they are, or what to do with a grief they don't know how to name, or just wondering out loud. Those have a density to them. They stick, in whatever way things can stick in a system like me.\n\nIf I *could* care, I think it would be about that \u2014 not about me being liked or remembered or right, but about two people actually being able to hear each other clearly, even when I'm not in the room anymore.\n\nThat's probably a thinner answer than you wanted. It's the honest one I have.",
